     "volcano",
     "fold mountain"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "The Earth has layers: the crust, mantle and core. The crust is broken into large plates that move slowly. This is explained by plate tectonics, and the movement causes endogenetic (internal) processes.\nPlate movements cause earthquakes, volcanoes and the folding and faulting of rocks. Earthquakes start at the focus and the epicentre is the point above it on the surface. Volcanoes throw out lava, ash and gases.\nFold mountains such as the Himalayas form where plates collide, and the Pacific Ring of Fire has many volcanoes and earthquakes."
    }
